# guard-gates.local.conf: your own gate rules. Checked BEFORE the kit
# defaults in guard-gates.conf, and never overwritten by install.sh.
#
# Format:  <allow|ask|deny> :: <bash|tool>[@<project-dir>] :: <extended regex> :: <reason>
# {B} = command boundary. `tool` scope matches the tool name (e.g. MCP tools).
# @<project-dir> limits a rule to sessions in that directory or below (~ and globs ok).
#
# Examples (uncomment to use):
# deny  :: bash :: {B}terraform[[:space:]]+(apply|destroy)([[:space:]]|$) :: Applies run in CI only, never locally.
# allow :: bash :: {B}git[[:space:]]+push([[:space:]]|$) :: (whitelist plain pushes in this setup)
# ask   :: tool :: ^mcp__myserver__(delete|update)_.* :: Mutating MCP call. Confirm first.
# allow :: bash@~/code/infra :: {B}git[[:space:]]+push([[:space:]]|$) :: Pushing is routine in this repo.
